      "test": "auxiliary_clauses::production_owned_decisions_relay_to_exact_caller_and_recover_after_disconnect",
      "assertions": [
        "An actual signed original native caller receives the committed session.accept/session.reject with its own request ID, original logical operation ID, CID/SID and original target by/capabilities/reason.",
        "A second physical peer using the same identity, credential and Device does not receive that caller relay.",
        "Logical replay uses a fresh native request correlation for the same immutable stored decision. It does not reinvite or repeat the decision.",
        "A decision may commit after caller disconnect; a newly authenticated caller can recover it by logical invitation replay.",
        "The original command mutation fence spans actual ACK output, so later relay read custody cannot enter its reply batch."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "implementation": [
    "Transient caller metadata binds a signed invitation invocation to its exact authenticated PeerAdmission and current route incarnation. It retains no authority reader, is bounded/expired and cannot survive as a physical channel after restart.",
    "Relay publication reacquires the dedicated caller read union under exact current credential/Device/key: original invitation receipt permission and actor epoch, recipient ceiling, original/current Session source access and target membership epoch. Binding/recipient metadata proofs cannot substitute.",
    "The immutable durable decision supplies by/capabilities/reason and Session scope. HTTP submissions create no native caller; native logical replay registers a new actual correlation and can relay a stored decision without another mutation.",
    "Verified current physical commands renew the current reachability lease while frozen older handles retain their original expiry. Pointer identity distinguishes physical peers sharing a Device.",
    "One attempt per caller request/target bounds uncertain notification IO. Application state remains authoritative in the journal/snapshot."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "No new complete clause count:16 of61 exact assigned clauses remain locally qualified;45 remain and G6-046 stays in progress.",
    "Clause0081 still needs the full Connection offer/answer, started and ended sequence; this component proves caller decision relay/recovery only.",
    "Correlated cancellation, started/joined/left observations, automatic loss/grace, interop URI targets and task-source G6-055 integration remain open.",
    "No Linux, production remote/browser/provider or named G6-093 qualification or publication. Upstream WebTransport/WSS fixtures qualify their recorded local reusable scope only.",
    "The earlier unresolved provider/consultation/retention observations are not relabeled passes."
  ],
